module

public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Limits.Shapes.Equalizers
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Sites.LeftExact
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.EquivalenceRelations
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Sheafification.LocalRepresentatives

/-!
# The quotient sheaf of a pre-relation

For a pre-relation on schemes over `S`, its *quotient presheaf* identifies two `T`-valued
points of `U` whenever they are the target and the source of a `T`-valued point of `R`.
The *quotient sheaf* is the sheafification of the quotient presheaf for a chosen topology.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Groupoids.points` is the functor of points of an `S`-scheme, restricted along a
  functor into `S`-schemes.
* `Stacks.Groupoids.sourceMap` and `Stacks.Groupoids.targetMap` are the two maps a
  pre-relation induces on functors of points.
* `Stacks.Groupoids.quotientPresheaf` is their pointwise coequalizer, and
  `Stacks.Groupoids.toQuotientPresheaf` is the canonical projection onto it.
* `Stacks.Groupoids.quotientSheaf` is the sheafification of the quotient presheaf, and
  `Stacks.Groupoids.toQuotientSheaf` is the canonical projection onto it.
* `Stacks.Groupoids.quotientSheafDesc` is the descent of a map which identifies related
  points, and `Stacks.Groupoids.quotientPresheafMap` and
  `Stacks.Groupoids.quotientSheafMap` are the maps induced by a morphism of
  pre-relations.
* `Stacks.Groupoids.quotientSheafMapIso` is the isomorphism of quotient sheaves induced by
  a morphism of pre-relations whose map of base objects is an isomorphism.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Groupoids.sourceMap_toQuotientSheaf` says that the projection coequalizes the
  source and target maps.
* `Stacks.Groupoids.isLocallySurjective_toQuotientSheaf`: the canonical projection onto the
  quotient sheaf is locally surjective, for every topology and with the objects and the
  morphisms of the site in universes unrelated to that of the schemes. Its sheafification
  half is `Stacks.Sheafification.isLocallySurjective_toSheafify_type`, which proves local
  surjectivity of the sheafification unit from the adjunction alone.
* `Stacks.Groupoids.toQuotientSheaf_quotientSheafDesc` and
  `Stacks.Groupoids.quotientSheafDesc_unique` are the universal property of the quotient
  sheaf.
* `Stacks.Groupoids.toQuotientSheaf_comp_quotientSheafMap` says that an induced map
  commutes with the canonical projections.
* `Stacks.Groupoids.quotientSheaf_hom_ext` says that a map out of a quotient sheaf is
  determined by its restriction to the functor of points of `U`, and
  `Stacks.Groupoids.quotientSheafMap_eq_of_obj_eq`,
  `Stacks.Groupoids.quotientSheafMap_comp` and `Stacks.Groupoids.quotientSheafMap_id`
  record the resulting functoriality of the construction.

## Implementation notes

The site is presented by an arbitrary functor into `S`-schemes, which covers the big and
small Zariski, étale, fppf, smooth and syntomic sites at once. Ordinary Yoneda keeps the
values of the functor of points in `Type u`, the universe of morphisms of `S`-schemes,
independently of the universe of the site's objects. The coequalizer of presheaves of
types is computed pointwise, so the quotient presheaf is exactly the quotient of
`Hom(T, U)` by the relation generated by `Hom(T, R)`; no equivalence-relation hypothesis
is needed to form it. For an action groupoid the same construction is written `U/G`.

The projection `Stacks.Groupoids.toQuotientSheaf` maps into the underlying presheaf of
the quotient sheaf, so its coequalizing property is available to maps of sheaves without
choosing a pointwise representative.

Mathlib's `CategoryTheory.Presheaf.isLocallySurjective_toSheafify` is an instance about
presheaves of `Type (max u v)` on a category of objects in `Type u` with morphisms in
`Type v`, so it does not fire for the quotient presheaf: the functor of points takes its
values in the universe of morphisms of `S`-schemes, which is unrelated to either universe of
the site. Local surjectivity of the unit is nevertheless formal, and
`Stacks.Sheafification.isLocallySurjective_toSheafify_type` proves it from the adjunction
alone, which is why local surjectivity of the projection needs no universe hypothesis
either.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 02VG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02VG)
-/

@[expose] public section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

universe u v w

namespace Stacks.Groupoids

variable {S : Scheme.{u}} {C : Type v} [Category.{w} C]

/-- The functor of points of an `S`-scheme `X`, restricted along a functor `F` presenting
a site of `S`-schemes. -/
abbrev points (F : C ⥤ Over S) (X : Over S) : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u :=
  F.op ⋙ yoneda.obj X

/-- The source map on the functors of points of a pre-relation. -/
noncomputable abbrev sourceMap (F : C ⥤ Over S) {R U : Over S}
    (j : PreRelation R U) : points F R ⟶ points F U :=
  F.op.whiskerLeft (yoneda.map j.source)

/-- The target map on the functors of points of a pre-relation. -/
noncomputable abbrev targetMap (F : C ⥤ Over S) {R U : Over S}
    (j : PreRelation R U) : points F R ⟶ points F U :=
  F.op.whiskerLeft (yoneda.map j.target)

/-- **Stacks 02VF.** The quotient presheaf of a pre-relation, the coequalizer of its two maps on
the restricted functors of points: it sends a test object `T` to the quotient of `U(T)` by the
equivalence relation generated by the image of `R(T)`. -/
@[implicit_reducible, stacks 02VF, sga "3 IV 3.1.2" "special case"]
noncomputable def quotientPresheaf (F : C ⥤ Over S) {R U : Over S}
    (j : PreRelation R U) : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u :=
  coequalizer (sourceMap F j) (targetMap F j)

/-- The projection of the functor of points of `U` onto the quotient presheaf. -/
noncomputable abbrev toQuotientPresheaf (F : C ⥤ Over S) {R U : Over S}
    (j : PreRelation R U) : points F U ⟶ quotientPresheaf F j :=
  coequalizer.π (sourceMap F j) (targetMap F j)

/-- **Stacks 02VG.** The *quotient sheaf* of a pre-relation, the sheafification of its
quotient presheaf. -/
@[stacks 02VG]
noncomputable abbrev quotientSheaf (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
    [HasSheafify J (Type u)] (F : C ⥤ Over S) {R U : Over S}
    (j : PreRelation R U) : Sheaf J (Type u) :=
  (presheafToSheaf J (Type u)).obj (quotientPresheaf F j)

/-- The canonical projection from the functor of points of `U` to its quotient sheaf. -/
noncomputable abbrev toQuotientSheaf (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
    [HasSheafify J (Type u)] (F : C ⥤ Over S) {R U : Over S}
    (j : PreRelation R U) : points F U ⟶ (quotientSheaf J F j).obj :=
  toQuotientPresheaf F j ≫ toSheafify J (quotientPresheaf F j)

/-- **The canonical projection onto the quotient sheaf of a pre-relation is locally
surjective**, for every topology on the site and with the objects and the morphisms of the
site in universes unrelated to that of the schemes. The projection onto the quotient presheaf
is a coequalizer projection, hence an epimorphism of presheaves of types and so pointwise
surjective, and the unit of the sheafification adjunction is locally surjective by
`Stacks.Sheafification.isLocallySurjective_toSheafify_type`. -/
theorem isLocallySurjective_toQuotientSheaf (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
    [HasSheafify J (Type u)] (F : C ⥤ Over S) {R U : Over S} (j : PreRelation R U) :
    Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J (toQuotientSheaf J F j) := by
  have hpre : Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J (toQuotientPresheaf F j) := by
    apply Presheaf.isLocallySurjective_of_surjective
    intro X
    have hepi : Epi (toQuotientPresheaf F j) := coequalizer.π_epi
    have : Epi ((toQuotientPresheaf F j).app X) := (NatTrans.epi_iff_epi_app _).1 hepi X
    exact surjective_of_epi _
  have := Stacks.Sheafification.isLocallySurjective_toSheafify_type J (quotientPresheaf F j)
  exact inferInstanceAs (Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J
    (toQuotientPresheaf F j ≫ toSheafify J (quotientPresheaf F j)))

/-- The canonical projection to the quotient sheaf identifies related points. -/
theorem sourceMap_toQuotientSheaf (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
    [HasSheafify J (Type u)] (F : C ⥤ Over S) {R U : Over S}
    (j : PreRelation R U) :
    sourceMap F j ≫ toQuotientSheaf J F j =
      targetMap F j ≫ toQuotientSheaf J F j := by
  unfold toQuotientSheaf toQuotientPresheaf
  rw [← Category.assoc, ← Category.assoc, coequalizer.condition]

/-- A map from the functor of points of `U` to a sheaf which identifies related points
descends to the quotient sheaf. -/
noncomputable def quotientSheafDesc (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
    [HasSheafify J (Type u)] (F : C ⥤ Over S) {R U : Over S}
    (j : PreRelation R U) (A : Sheaf J (Type u))
    (k : points F U ⟶ A.obj)
    (h : sourceMap F j ≫ k = targetMap F j ≫ k) :
    quotientSheaf J F j ⟶ A :=
  ⟨sheafifyLift J (coequalizer.desc k h) A.property⟩

/-- The descended map agrees with the original map on the functor of points of `U`. -/
theorem toQuotientSheaf_quotientSheafDesc (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
    [HasSheafify J (Type u)] (F : C ⥤ Over S) {R U : Over S}
    (j : PreRelation R U) (A : Sheaf J (Type u))
    (k : points F U ⟶ A.obj)
    (h : sourceMap F j ≫ k = targetMap F j ≫ k) :
    toQuotientSheaf J F j ≫ (quotientSheafDesc J F j A k h).hom = k := by
  change toQuotientPresheaf F j ≫ toSheafify J (quotientPresheaf F j) ≫
    sheafifyLift J (coequalizer.desc k h) A.property = k
  rw [toSheafify_sheafifyLift]
  exact coequalizer.π_desc k h

/-- Descent from the quotient sheaf is unique. -/
theorem quotientSheafDesc_unique (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
    [HasSheafify J (Type u)] (F : C ⥤ Over S) {R U : Over S}
    (j : PreRelation R U) (A : Sheaf J (Type u))
    (k : points F U ⟶ A.obj)
    (h : sourceMap F j ≫ k = targetMap F j ≫ k)
    (d : quotientSheaf J F j ⟶ A)
    (hd : toQuotientSheaf J F j ≫ d.hom = k) :
    d = quotientSheafDesc J F j A k h :=
  Sheaf.hom_ext <| sheafify_hom_ext J _ _ A.property <| coequalizer.hom_ext <|
    hd.trans (toQuotientSheaf_quotientSheafDesc J F j A k h).symm

/-- A morphism of pre-relations induces a morphism of quotient presheaves. -/
noncomputable def quotientPresheafMap (F : C ⥤ Over S)
    {R U R' U' : Over S} (j : PreRelation R U)
    (j' : PreRelation R' U') (r : R ⟶ R') (f : U ⟶ U')
    (hs : r ≫ j'.source = j.source ≫ f)
    (ht : r ≫ j'.target = j.target ≫ f) :
    quotientPresheaf F j ⟶ quotientPresheaf F j' := by
  let rf : points F R ⟶ points F R' := F.op.whiskerLeft (yoneda.map r)
  let ff : points F U ⟶ points F U' := F.op.whiskerLeft (yoneda.map f)
  refine coequalizer.desc (ff ≫ toQuotientPresheaf F j') ?_
  have hsource : sourceMap F j ≫ ff = rf ≫ sourceMap F j' := by
    dsimp [sourceMap, ff, rf]
    rw [← Functor.whiskerLeft_comp, ← Functor.whiskerLeft_comp, ← Functor.map_comp,
      ← Functor.map_comp, hs]
  have htarget : targetMap F j ≫ ff = rf ≫ targetMap F j' := by
    dsimp [targetMap, ff, rf]
    rw [← Functor.whiskerLeft_comp, ← Functor.whiskerLeft_comp, ← Functor.map_comp,
      ← Functor.map_comp, ht]
  simp only [← Category.assoc, hsource, htarget, toQuotientPresheaf]
  rw [Category.assoc, Category.assoc, coequalizer.condition]

/-- The map of quotient sheaves induced by a morphism of pre-relations. -/
noncomputable abbrev quotientSheafMap (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
    [HasSheafify J (Type u)] (F : C ⥤ Over S)
    {R U R' U' : Over S} (j : PreRelation R U)
    (j' : PreRelation R' U') (r : R ⟶ R') (f : U ⟶ U')
    (hs : r ≫ j'.source = j.source ≫ f)
    (ht : r ≫ j'.target = j.target ≫ f) :
    quotientSheaf J F j ⟶ quotientSheaf J F j' :=
  (presheafToSheaf J (Type u)).map (quotientPresheafMap F j j' r f hs ht)

/-- The induced morphism of quotient sheaves commutes with the canonical projections. -/
theorem toQuotientSheaf_comp_quotientSheafMap
    (J : GrothendieckTopology C) [HasSheafify J (Type u)]
    (F : C ⥤ Over S) {R U R' U' : Over S}
    (j : PreRelation R U) (j' : PreRelation R' U')
    (r : R ⟶ R') (f : U ⟶ U')
    (hs : r ≫ j'.source = j.source ≫ f)
    (ht : r ≫ j'.target = j.target ≫ f) :
    toQuotientSheaf J F j ≫ (quotientSheafMap J F j j' r f hs ht).hom =
      (F.op.whiskerLeft (yoneda.map f)) ≫ toQuotientSheaf J F j' := by
  rw [toQuotientSheaf, quotientSheafMap]
  change toQuotientPresheaf F j ≫ toSheafify J (quotientPresheaf F j) ≫
      sheafifyMap J (quotientPresheafMap F j j' r f hs ht) = _
  rw [← toSheafify_naturality]
  change (coequalizer.π (sourceMap F j) (targetMap F j)) ≫
      quotientPresheafMap F j j' r f hs ht ≫ _ = _
  rw [← Category.assoc, quotientPresheafMap, coequalizer.π_desc]
  rfl

/-- Two maps out of a quotient sheaf agree as soon as they agree on the functor of points of
`U`, the canonical projection onto the quotient sheaf being an epimorphism. -/
theorem quotientSheaf_hom_ext (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
    [HasSheafify J (Type u)] (F : C ⥤ Over S) {R U : Over S}
    (j : PreRelation R U) (A : Sheaf J (Type u))
    (a b : quotientSheaf J F j ⟶ A)
    (h : toQuotientSheaf J F j ≫ a.hom = toQuotientSheaf J F j ≫ b.hom) : a = b :=
  Sheaf.hom_ext <| sheafify_hom_ext J _ _ A.property <| coequalizer.hom_ext h

/-- The induced map of quotient sheaves is the unique map compatible with the projections. -/
private theorem quotientSheafMap_eq_of_comp_eq (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
    [HasSheafify J (Type u)] (F : C ⥤ Over S) {R U R' U' : Over S}
    (j : PreRelation R U) (j' : PreRelation R' U') (r : R ⟶ R') (f : U ⟶ U')
    (hs : r ≫ j'.source = j.source ≫ f) (ht : r ≫ j'.target = j.target ≫ f)
    (g : quotientSheaf J F j ⟶ quotientSheaf J F j')
    (h : F.op.whiskerLeft (yoneda.map f) ≫ toQuotientSheaf J F j' =
      toQuotientSheaf J F j ≫ g.hom) :
    quotientSheafMap J F j j' r f hs ht = g :=
  quotientSheaf_hom_ext J F j _ _ _ (by rw [toQuotientSheaf_comp_quotientSheafMap]; exact h)

/-- The induced map of quotient sheaves depends only on the map of base objects: two
morphisms of pre-relations lying over the same map `U ⟶ U'` induce the same map. -/
theorem quotientSheafMap_eq_of_obj_eq (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
    [HasSheafify J (Type u)] (F : C ⥤ Over S) {R U R' U' : Over S}
    (j : PreRelation R U) (j' : PreRelation R' U')
    (r r' : R ⟶ R') (f f' : U ⟶ U')
    (hs : r ≫ j'.source = j.source ≫ f) (ht : r ≫ j'.target = j.target ≫ f)
    (hs' : r' ≫ j'.source = j.source ≫ f') (ht' : r' ≫ j'.target = j.target ≫ f')
    (hf : f = f') :
    quotientSheafMap J F j j' r f hs ht = quotientSheafMap J F j j' r' f' hs' ht' := by
  subst hf
  exact quotientSheafMap_eq_of_comp_eq J F j j' r f hs ht _
    (toQuotientSheaf_comp_quotientSheafMap J F j j' r' f hs' ht').symm

/-- The maps of quotient sheaves induced by two composable morphisms of pre-relations
compose. -/
theorem quotientSheafMap_comp (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
    [HasSheafify J (Type u)] (F : C ⥤ Over S) {R₀ U₀ R₁ U₁ R₂ U₂ : Over S}
    (j₀ : PreRelation R₀ U₀) (j₁ : PreRelation R₁ U₁) (j₂ : PreRelation R₂ U₂)
    (r₀ : R₀ ⟶ R₁) (f₀ : U₀ ⟶ U₁)
    (hs₀ : r₀ ≫ j₁.source = j₀.source ≫ f₀)
    (ht₀ : r₀ ≫ j₁.target = j₀.target ≫ f₀)
    (r₁ : R₁ ⟶ R₂) (f₁ : U₁ ⟶ U₂)
    (hs₁ : r₁ ≫ j₂.source = j₁.source ≫ f₁)
    (ht₁ : r₁ ≫ j₂.target = j₁.target ≫ f₁) :
    quotientSheafMap J F j₀ j₁ r₀ f₀ hs₀ ht₀ ≫ quotientSheafMap J F j₁ j₂ r₁ f₁ hs₁ ht₁ =
      quotientSheafMap J F j₀ j₂ (r₀ ≫ r₁) (f₀ ≫ f₁)
        (by rw [Category.assoc, hs₁, ← Category.assoc, hs₀, Category.assoc])
        (by rw [Category.assoc, ht₁, ← Category.assoc, ht₀, Category.assoc]) :=
  (quotientSheafMap_eq_of_comp_eq J F j₀ j₂ (r₀ ≫ r₁) (f₀ ≫ f₁) _ _ _ (by
    refine Eq.trans ?_ (Category.assoc (toQuotientSheaf J F j₀) _ _).symm
    rw [← Category.assoc (toQuotientSheaf J F j₀), toQuotientSheaf_comp_quotientSheafMap,
      Category.assoc, toQuotientSheaf_comp_quotientSheafMap]
    simp)).symm

/-- The identity morphism of a pre-relation induces the identity of its quotient sheaf. -/
theorem quotientSheafMap_id (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
    [HasSheafify J (Type u)] (F : C ⥤ Over S) {R U : Over S} (j : PreRelation R U) :
    quotientSheafMap J F j j (𝟙 R) (𝟙 U) (by simp) (by simp) = 𝟙 _ :=
  quotientSheafMap_eq_of_comp_eq J F j j _ _ _ _ _ (by simp)

/-- A morphism of pre-relations whose map of base objects is an isomorphism induces an
isomorphism of quotient sheaves: the induced map depends only on that base map. -/
noncomputable def quotientSheafMapIso (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
    [HasSheafify J (Type u)] (F : C ⥤ Over S) {R U R' U' : Over S}
    (j : PreRelation R U) (j' : PreRelation R' U')
    (r : R ⟶ R') (f : U ⟶ U') (rInv : R' ⟶ R) (fInv : U' ⟶ U)
    (hs : r ≫ j'.source = j.source ≫ f) (ht : r ≫ j'.target = j.target ≫ f)
    (hsInv : rInv ≫ j.source = j'.source ≫ fInv)
    (htInv : rInv ≫ j.target = j'.target ≫ fInv)
    (hf : f ≫ fInv = 𝟙 U) (hfInv : fInv ≫ f = 𝟙 U') :
    quotientSheaf J F j ≅ quotientSheaf J F j' where
  hom := quotientSheafMap J F j j' r f hs ht
  inv := quotientSheafMap J F j' j rInv fInv hsInv htInv
  hom_inv_id := by
    rw [quotientSheafMap_comp]
    exact (quotientSheafMap_eq_of_obj_eq J F j j
      (r ≫ rInv) (𝟙 R) (f ≫ fInv) (𝟙 U) _ _ _ _ (by simpa using hf)).trans
        (quotientSheafMap_id J F j)
  inv_hom_id := by
    rw [quotientSheafMap_comp]
    exact (quotientSheafMap_eq_of_obj_eq J F j' j'
      (rInv ≫ r) (𝟙 R') (fInv ≫ f) (𝟙 U') _ _ _ _ (by simpa using hfInv)).trans
        (quotientSheafMap_id J F j')

end Stacks.Groupoids

end
